      "verifiedSourceLocator": {
        "htmlSection": "Respecting the Representative Body; Respecting the Meetings of the Legislative Body",
        "section": "代表机构与立法会议 / Representative body and legislative meetings; printed pp. 13–14"
      },
      "reviewNotes": "Direct evidence here is the acquired constitutional text and its prescribed record books. The formal_legal_code variable permits a unified oral legal system as well as a written one; its Chinese label follows the project’s 正式法律体系 rather than reducing the category to written codes. It does not prove that every meeting produced a surviving volume. Electoral details are left by the constitution to law; no universal franchise, actual seat totals, or fully separated modern branches are inferred. Both Polaris observations remain undated.",
