      "verifiedSourceLocator": {
        "htmlSection": "Respecting the Tax Officers",
        "section": "税官条款 / Tax officers; archive scan pp. 6–7 (printed pp. 14–15)"
      },
      "reviewNotes": "The constitution describes appointment, accountability and a payment route, not employment hours or an independently counted Seshat hierarchy. Both full_time_bureaucrat rows are deliberately associated because 1840 appears in both; no interval endpoint is repaired, no SA value is discarded, and no present/absent decision is derived from this text. Tax and land jurisdiction is separately distinguishable from ordinary judges.",
